<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Primac in suit vs revised IAMA Part A.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Primac in suit vs revised IAMA Part A.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rural services group Primac Holdings Ltd said it launched on Wednesday legal action to prevent the dispatch of the revised Part A takeover offer by spurned suitor IAMA Ltd.</p>
<p>Fellow rural services group, IAMA, is offering nine of its shares for every 10 Primac shares, an offer which Primac directors have said appeared to be inadequate.</p>
<p>Based on IAMA's closing prices of A$2.88, the offer values Primac at A$2.592 compared to a Primac closing price of A$2.86.</p>
<p>Primac said it believed the revised Part A statement did not comply with Corporations Law disclosure requirements.  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
